+++
title = "Template Functions"
template = "docs"
+++

Revela themes are [Scriban](https://github.com/scriban/scriban) templates (`.revela` files). Every template has access to the built-in functions below for URLs, images, date/EXIF formatting, UI text, and Markdown. For where these are used, see [Theme Customization](../../guide/themes/).

<div class="features-grid">

### 🖼️ Images

`find_image`, `variant_url`: resolve images and build variant URLs.

### 🔗 URLs

`page_url`, `absolute_url`, `asset_url`: generate page, absolute, and asset links.

### 📅 Formatting

`format_date`, `format_filesize`, `format_exif_*`: human-readable values.

### 🌍 Text

`t`, `html_escape`: theme UI text in the site language, safe escaping.

### 📝 Content

`markdown`: render Markdown to HTML.

</div>

---

## Image Functions

### `find_image`

Resolve an image from the project by path. Uses the same 3-step lookup as Markdown content images.

```scriban
{{~ logo = find_image "logo.jpg" ~}}
{{~ if logo ~}}
<img src="{{ variant_url(logo, 640, 'jpg') }}"
     width="{{ logo.width }}" height="{{ logo.height }}">
{{~ end ~}}
```

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `path` | string | Image path (relative to gallery, `_images/`, or exact) |

**Returns** an `Image` object (or `null` if not found). Resolution order:

1. Gallery-local: `{current gallery path}/{path}`
2. Shared images: `_images/{path}`
3. Exact match: `{path}` as-is

The `Image` object exposes `slug`, `width`, `height`, `sizes`, `file_size`, `date_taken`, `exif`, `title`, `description`, `tags`, and `placeholder`.

### `variant_url`

Build a URL for a specific image variant (size + format), resolved against the current page's asset base path.

```scriban
{{ variant_url(image, 1920, "webp") }}
```

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `image` | Image | Image object (e.g. from `images` or `find_image`) |
| `size` | int | Target width |
| `format` | string | `"avif"`, `"webp"`, or `"jpg"` |

**Returns** `{assets_basepath}{image.slug}/{size}.{format}`, e.g. `../images/events/fireworks/029081/1920.webp`.

Choose a size from `image.sizes` and a format from `image_formats`; the helper
does not generate missing variants. Configured asset prefixes must end with `/`.

### `absolute_variant_url`

Generate an absolute image-variant URL for Open Graph or other image metadata in
a full page template. It respects the current gallery/photo page, deployment
prefix and asset base path, including absolute CDN addresses.

```scriban
{{ og_size = image.sizes | array.last }}
<meta property="og:image" content="{{ html_escape (absolute_variant_url image og_size 'jpg') }}">
```

Social crawlers prefer JPEG around 1200–1920 px; Lumina's `Partials/OpenGraphImage.revela`
picks the largest generated size up to 1920 and also emits `og:image:width`/`og:image:height`.

Without `base_url`, local variants use a root-relative URL; an absolute CDN URL
remains absolute. This helper needs the normal page context (`base_url`,
`basepath`, `assets_basepath`, and `gallery` or `photo`/`image`). Separately rendered
content-image partials only have the asset context: use `variant_url` there.
`absolute_url(image)` still links to the canonical **photo page**, not its image file.

---

## URL Functions

### `page_url`

Generate a URL for a page. Polymorphic — accepts an `Image`, `Gallery`, `NavigationItem`, or a slug string. Returns `null` for a navigation item that has no page (a section header), so templates can branch on it.

```scriban
{{ page_url(gallery) }}
{{ page_url("gallery/vacation") }}
```

**Returns** a site-relative URL, e.g. `/gallery/vacation/` (relative to the current page's base path).

### `absolute_url`

Generate an absolute URL (including host from `project.baseUrl` and the deployment prefix) for Open Graph, RSS, sitemap, or JSON-LD. Same polymorphism as `page_url`. When `baseUrl` is unset it returns the root-relative form instead of failing. Escape helper results with `html_escape` when writing HTML attributes.

```scriban
{{ absolute_url(gallery) }}
```

**Returns** e.g. `https://example.com/gallery/vacation/` (or `/gallery/vacation/` without `baseUrl`).

### `asset_url`

Generate a URL for a theme asset (CSS, JS).

```scriban
{{ asset_url "css/style.css" }}
```

**Returns** the asset path relative to the current page, including the site base path: `_assets/css/style.css` on the home page, `../_assets/css/style.css` one level down, or `/gallery/_assets/css/style.css` with an absolute base path of `/gallery/`.

---

## Formatting Functions

### `format_date`

Format a date with a custom format string. Month and day names follow `language` in `site.json` (`"de"` turns `MMMM` into `März`); an unknown language falls back to neutral (English) names.

```scriban
{{ format_date image.date_taken "yyyy-MM-dd" }}
{{ format_date image.date_taken "MMMM yyyy" }}
```

### `format_filesize`

Format a byte count as a human-readable string, using the number format of the site language.

```scriban
{{ format_filesize image.file_size }}
```

**Returns** e.g. `"2.4 MB"`, `"340 KB"` (`"2,4 MB"` for `"language": "de"`).

### `format_exif_exposure`

Format an exposure time as photography notation.

```scriban
{{ format_exif_exposure image.exif.exposure_time }}
```

**Returns** e.g. `"1/500s"`, `"0.5s"`, `"10s"` (or `"N/A"` when unset).

### `format_exif_aperture`

Format an aperture (f-number) as photography notation.

```scriban
{{ format_exif_aperture image.exif.f_number }}
```

**Returns** e.g. `"f/2.8"`, `"f/11"` (or `"N/A"` when unset).

---

## Text Functions

### `t`

Return a theme UI string (button labels, headings, screen-reader text) in the site language.
Strings come from the theme's `Locales/<language>.json` files; see
[Theme Language](../../guide/themes/#theme-language).

```scriban
<button aria-label="{{ html_escape (t 'photo.close') }}">&times;</button>
<a aria-label="{{ html_escape (t 'photo.return_to' gallery.title) }}">…</a>
```

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `key` | string | Namespaced key, e.g. `photo.close`, `statistics.overview` |
| `args…` | any | Optional values for the placeholders `{0}`, `{1}`, … |

**Returns** plain text. The value of `language` in `site.json` is tried exactly
(`de-CH`), then without region (`de`), then `en`; a key missing everywhere
renders as the key itself so the gap is visible. Placeholder values are inserted
culture-invariantly.

The result is **not** trusted HTML: arguments are often user data such as gallery
titles. Always escape it like any other text, e.g. `html_escape (t "key" value)`.

### `html_escape`

Escape text for HTML content and quoted attribute values. Scriban does not escape
automatically, so wrap every dynamic value (titles, EXIF data, `t` results, URLs).

```scriban
<img alt="{{ html_escape image.title }}" src="{{ html_escape (variant_url image 640 'jpg') }}">
```

**Returns** the text with only `&`, `<`, `>`, `"` and `'` replaced (`&amp;`, `&lt;`, `&gt;`,
`&quot;`, `&#39;`). Everything else, including umlauts and other non-ASCII characters, stays
literal (`Menü`, not `Men&#252;`); generated pages are UTF-8.

---

## Content Functions

### `markdown`

Convert Markdown text to HTML. Works as a function or a filter.

```scriban
{{ "**bold** text" | markdown }}
```

**Returns** `<p><strong>bold</strong> text</p>`.

---

## Template Variables

These values (not functions) are available in templates:

| Variable | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `site` | object | Site settings from `site.json` |
| `gallery` | Gallery | Current page (`title`, `body`, `cover_image`, `template`) |
| `galleries` | Gallery[] | Child galleries (home page only) |
| `images` | Image[] | Images for the current gallery |
| `nav_items` | NavItem[] | Navigation tree with active state |
| `basepath` | string | Path to the site root: relative (`""`, `"../"`), or your absolute `basePath`; always root-absolute on the 404 page |
| `assets_basepath` | string | Path/URL to image variants |
| `base_url` | string? | Absolute site host from `project.baseUrl` (null when unset) |
| `og_locale` | string | Open Graph locale from `language` in `site.json` (`"de"` → `de_DE`; empty when unknown) |
| `not_found` | bool | `true` only while rendering `404.html` (`Body/NotFound.revela`) |
| `image_formats` | string[] | Active formats (`["avif", "webp", "jpg"]`) |
| `page_content` | string | Rendered Markdown body (gallery pages) |
| `stylesheets` | string[] | CSS filenames resolved for the current template, plugin, and feature scopes |
| `scripts` | string[] | JS filenames resolved for the current template, plugin, and feature scopes |
| `revela` | object | Build info: `revela.version`, `revela.kind`, `revela.framework`, `revela.configuration` |

`stylesheets` and `scripts` are already filtered before the template is rendered. Templates
should emit the provided filenames in order; they do not need to inspect page scopes or asset
configuration themselves. Canonical photo pages receive only the scoped image zoom script;
Lightbox pages receive both dialog behavior and image zoom scripts.

